      "explanation": "For good quality cement, the ratio of lime (CaO) to the sum of the oxides of silicon (SiO₂), aluminum (Al₂O₃), and iron (Fe₂O₃) should be approximately 2:1.\n<br/><br/>\nThis proportion ensures that the cement has good strength and setting properties, as well as resistance to chemical attack."
